 "changesFromC1007": [
  "Alt text follows KAN-59/11405 as accepted for the live registry in 11511: \"Xenios {name} {amount} packaging design\" and \"Front label artwork for Xenios {name} {amount}\", with no form or container wording. write_manifest.py writes it and verify_c1.py binds each website role to it and refuses form wording (KAN-31/11570). verify_c1.py also counts ng, pg, nanogram and picogram as mass units that an IU record must not print.",
  "build_c1.py and xr_compose.py carry Root's Option B layout for blend names (KAN-59/11404). This batch has no blend, and with these copies every label master, name fit and layout of C1-001 to C1-007 is unchanged (753 of 753 compared), and C1-006 and C1-007 rebuild byte for byte. svg_label_render.py and wpf_kern.ps1 are byte-identical to C1-007's copies.",
  "This is the first batch whose amounts are in IU; each prints as the label facts give it, with no mass unit anywhere. c1_variants.py adds the reference of the adopted label facts (KAN-59/11584) and HCG's per-compound do-not-print terms. write_manifest.py records this batch's claim reference and this note. The kern table covers the strings in this batch.",
  "2 of 2 records have form-neutral label facts: they state the name, the amount with its unit, the product code and the classification, and no form. For those records the printed vial and the per-vial amount basis rest on the packaging declaration alone; labelFacts keeps the hold note and formBasis cites the declaration."
 ],
